CAT = "fihygLaw"; SEG = "LAW"
Q = [
("Which Finnish law sets the main rules for food safety and food control?",
 "The Food Act", ["The Road Traffic Act", "The Hunting Act", "The Copyright Act"],
 "The Food Act (297/2021) and the decrees under it, together with EU food hygiene regulations, set the rules for food businesses and food control in Finland."),
("Which national authority steers food control and maintains the Hygiene Passport system?",
 "Ruokavirasto", ["Traficom", "The Tax Administration", "Kela"],
 "Ruokavirasto steers food control across Finland and approves the examiners who issue Hygiene Passports. Local food control units do the inspections."),
("Who needs a Hygiene Passport under the Food Act?",
 "Anyone handling unpackaged perishables", ["Every cashier in any shop", "Only restaurant owners", "Only food delivery drivers"],
 "The Food Act requires a Hygiene Passport from people who handle unpackaged, easily perishable food on food premises, for example in cafes, restaurants and food factories."),
("How long may a new worker handle unpackaged perishable food before needing a Hygiene Passport?",
 "Up to three months", ["Up to one week", "Up to one year", "Up to two years"],
 "The Food Act requires the passport once a person has worked at least three months in such tasks. Earlier jobs that needed a passport count towards the three months."),
("What must an employer keep about the food hygiene competence of its staff?",
 "A record of it", ["Nothing at all", "Copies of staff tax cards", "Their school reports"],
 "The Food Act requires food business operators to keep a record of the food hygiene competence of the people working on their premises and show it to the inspector on request."),
("A worker has a food hygiene certificate from another country. What applies in Finland?",
 "It does not count in Finland", ["It replaces the passport", "It counts for one year", "It must only be translated"],
 "Hygiene certificates issued abroad do not count as a Finnish Hygiene Passport. The worker must show competence with the Finnish passport."),
("What must a new restaurant do before it starts operating?",
 "Notify food control", ["Nothing, it may just open", "Apply for a state grant", "Register with the police"],
 "A restaurant is a registered food business: before starting it sends a notification, with a description of its self-monitoring and a floor plan, to the local food control authority."),
("Which EU regulation sets general hygiene rules for all food businesses?",
 "Regulation (EC) 852/2004", ["The GDPR", "The Working Time Directive", "The Driving Licence Directive"],
 "Regulation (EC) No 852/2004 on the hygiene of foodstuffs applies directly in Finland alongside the Food Act and its decrees."),
("What does the term food hygiene cover?",
 "Everything keeping food safe", ["Only washing the dishes", "Only staff showers", "Only how food tastes"],
 "Food hygiene means every action and condition needed to keep food safe and fit to eat, from raw materials to serving. That is why everyone handling food needs basic competence."),
("Which statement about food control authorities is true?",
 "They may inspect and sample", ["They may only phone the owner", "They need the owner's consent", "They check only the prices"],
 "Under the Food Act the control authority has the right to inspect food premises, take samples and see self-monitoring records, and can order corrections."),
]
